.policy "ruff-arg003-unused-class-method-argument" revision 2
.description "Remove class method parameters the body never reads, or prefix them with an underscore when the signature must stay and no caller passes them by keyword."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff ARG003 (flake8-unused-arguments): a class method's parameter that the body never reads. `cls` is left
// out, and so are names matching dummy-variable-rgx. A class method is decorated @classmethod (or
// abc.abstractclassmethod); `__init_subclass__` and `__class_getitem__` are implicit ones, but as dunders they
// are not checked. Stubs, @abstractmethod, @override, @overload and defs that call `locals()` are skipped.
//   class C:
//       @classmethod
//       def f(cls, x): print(1)         ← ARG003 at x
#include "python/misc2-args.rr"
//   options: dummy-variable-rgx, flake8-unused-arguments.ignore-variadic-names (see the library)

.violation ARG003(at: node, name: symbol) code "ARG003"
    "Remove `{name}` if no caller passes it. If the signature must stay, such as to match a base class, prefix it with an underscore, but keep the name when callers pass it by keyword."
    suppress ruff "ARG003"
ARG003(nm, x) :- arg_unused(_, nm, x, "ARG003").
